{"name":"Harmonious Gold","hex":"#eacfa3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"harmonious","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Showing accord in feeling or action.","Having components pleasingly or appropriately combined."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/harmonious"},{"term":"gold","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A heavy yellow elemental metal of great value, with atomic number 79.","A coin or coinage made of this material, or supposedly so."]},{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["☉ (alchemy)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gold"}],"entries":[{"title":"Harmonious (Epcot)","blocks":[{"text":"Harmonious was a multimedia, fireworks-based nighttime spectacular at EPCOT at Walt Disney World Resort in Bay Lake, Florida. Intended as the long-term replacement for IllumiNations: Reflections of Earth, Harmonious showcased and celebrated the cultures and stories of the world that have inspired various Disney films and music, and how it can unite us all, overcoming any language or border. The show utilized pyrotechnics, choreographed water fountains, water curtains, lasers, searchlights, and LED screens to present a 360° audio-visual experience on the park's World Showcase Lagoon. The primary show equipment was notably housed on a collective of floating barges that were permanently moored at the center of the lagoon. Before its retirement, Harmonious was described as the largest nighttime spectacular ever created by Disney Live Entertainment."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Harmonious_Opening_Night_%2851537996565%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Harmonious_Opening_Night_%2851537996565%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harmonious_(Epcot)","wikidata":"Q108801741"},{"title":"Gold","blocks":[{"text":"Gold is a chemical element; its chemical symbol is Au and atomic number 79. In its pure form, it is a bright-metallic-yellow, dense, soft, malleable, and ductile metal. Chemically, gold is a transition metal, a group 11 element, and one of the noble metals. It is one of the least reactive chemical elements, being the second lowest in the reactivity series, with only platinum ranked as less reactive. Gold is solid under standard conditions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Gold-crystals.jpg/330px-Gold-crystals.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold","wikidata":"Q897"},{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_(color)","wikidata":"Q208045"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Harmonious_Centerpiece_Barge_at_EPCOT.jpg/500px-Harmonious_Centerpiece_Barge_at_EPCOT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Harmonious_Centerpiece_Barge_at_EPCOT.jpg/1280px-Harmonious_Centerpiece_Barge_at_EPCOT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Harmonious_Centerpiece_Barge_at_EPCOT.jpg/500px-Harmonious_Centerpiece_Barge_at_EPCOT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The show's centerpiece platform with water curtain and fountain nozzles activated, as seen during the post show sequence.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHarmonious_Centerpiece_Barge_at_EPCOT.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Harmonious_show_barges_daytime%2C_EPCOT.jpg/500px-Harmonious_show_barges_daytime%2C_EPCOT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Harmonious_show_barges_daytime%2C_EPCOT.jpg/1280px-Harmonious_show_barges_daytime%2C_EPCOT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Harmonious_show_barges_daytime%2C_EPCOT.jpg/500px-Harmonious_show_barges_daytime%2C_EPCOT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The show's five main barges seen during the daytime.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHarmonious_show_barges_daytime%2C_EPCOT.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/55/EPCOT_Harmonious_Soundtrack.jpg/250px-EPCOT_Harmonious_Soundtrack.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/55/EPCOT_Harmonious_Soundtrack.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/55/EPCOT_Harmonious_Soundtrack.jpg/250px-EPCOT_Harmonious_Soundtrack.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEPCOT_Harmonious_Soundtrack.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d5/Beowulf_-_gold.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d5/Beowulf_-_gold.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"The word gold in the Beowulf manuscript","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABeowulf_-_gold.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Small_gold_nugget_5mm_dia_and_corresponding_foil_surface_of_half_sq_meter.jpg/500px-Small_gold_nugge